Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(sefariasqlite): re-anchor the Ramban on Shabbat 141b
 link to the lines it explains (Otzaria/otzaria#4023)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sefaria links Chiddushei Ramban on Shabbat 141b:2 ("א"ה מאי איריא אבן אפי' דינר נמי") to
Shabbat 141b:16 ("...מאי איריא רפוי"), so the Ramban shows only when the whole daf is selected.
The dibbur explains Shabbat 141b:28 ("אי הכי,") and 142a:1 ("מאי איריא אבן, אפילו דינר נמי!").

New resource corrected_link_citations.tsv (SefariaLinkCitationCorrections): an exact Sefaria row
whose one side is wrong gets a reviewed replacement before resolution, in either column order. The
replacement here is the range Shabbat 141b:28-142a:1, so the importer writes the link on 141b:28
with link_range/link_coverage through 142a:1. A row Sefaria has since changed is left alone and
logged as an unused correction.
